Source: Rhode Island General Assembly, https://webserver.rilegislature.gov/ (read from Internet Archive captures; retrieved 2026-11-10).

Statute and constitution text is not copyrightable: under the government edicts doctrine, as the Supreme Court applied it
in Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, Inc., 590 U.S. 255 (2020), no one holds copyright in the laws that legislators make in
their official capacity. No annotations are used.

